\title{Events}
\description{
Everything that happens in a termr application is an event: key
presses, terminal resizes, focus changes, widgets being mounted, and
messages that widgets send (such as \code{"button.pressed"}).

Events are delivered to their \emph{target} widget and, if they bubble, to
each ancestor in turn and finally to the \link{App}. Any handler can call
\code{event$stop()} to stop propagation.

Event types and their classes:
\itemize{
\item \code{"key"}: \code{KeyEvent} with fields \code{key}, \code{char}, \code{ctrl}, \code{alt}, \code{shift};
\item \code{"resize"}: \code{ResizeEvent} with \code{width} and \code{height};
\item \code{"paste"}: \code{PasteEvent} with the pasted \code{text} (bracketed paste);
\item \code{"focus"} / \code{"blur"}: \code{FocusEvent} / \code{BlurEvent} (do not bubble);
\item \code{"mount"} / \code{"unmount"}: \code{MountEvent} / \code{UnmountEvent} (do not bubble);
\item any other name: \code{MessageEvent}, created by \code{widget$post_message()}.
}
}
